# FreeInference's Compose-level settings.
#
# Separate from backend.env/frontend.env because these configure Compose
# itself rather than a service. The deploy scripts glob deploy/*.env into
# `docker compose --env-file` (see ops/deploy/*.sh and the Makefile's
# DISTRIBUTION_ENV_FILES), so a file added here is picked up automatically.

# pgAdmin sits behind the `admin` profile, so nothing starts it unless a
# profile is named. It was never named, which is why the console's pgAdmin
# link had nothing to reach.
#
# This file is the declaration; `--env-file` is not how it gets there. Compose
# ignored COMPOSE_PROFILES inside an `--env-file` from 2.27.1 until the fix for
# docker/compose#11856, so the deploy scripts read this line themselves and
# export it (`export_compose_profiles`), which every version honours. They
# union it with whatever the host's own `.env` selects, so a host that also
# runs oncall keeps it without having to restate `admin` here.
#
# Running Compose by hand is the one case that depends on the `--env-file`
# path, and on an affected version a host `.env` that sets COMPOSE_PROFILES
# wins outright there — list every profile you want in that case.
COMPOSE_PROFILES=admin
